<title>VENEZUELA: Enron's Ventane reports 9-mo net $917,000.</title>
<headline>Enron's Ventane reports 9-mo net $917,000.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan affiliate of U.S. energy company Enron Corp, Industrias Ventane SA, reported inflation-adjusted nine month net profits for the period ending September 30 of 254 million bolivars ($540,000).</p>
<p>Comparative inflation-adjusted 1995 results for Venezuela's leading liquid gas company, which is 80 percent owned by Enron, were not available, the company said.</p>
<p>Net sales for the period were 18.2 billion bolivars, while costs of sales stood at 5.7 billion bolivars and operating and administrative costs at 10.6 billion bolivars, the press release showed.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
